# Reminder-only beat for demo step 4: the truncated log, no root type.
#
# A single step: the script pane summarizes the whole operation and the
# presenter drives protolens by hand (fold, G, i, o, t, /). Reverse-
# crafting a schema for an unknown blob from the fields the corpus does
# know. Advance (to quit) with space or Enter.
#
# Invocation (from grehack2026.sh):
#   protolens --descriptor-set life.desc eve/server.log \
#       --script beats/logfile

title: A blob with no schema

steps:
  - text: |
      eve/server.log, opened against life.desc — no known root type
      matches, so the root is a generic `message`. Walk the recovery:

      1. Fold to depth 1 (`1`), then `G` to the end — the tail is flagged
         TRUNCATED. That is why protoc --decode_raw choked on the whole
         file.

      2. Fold to depth 2 (`2`), turn on heat cues (`i`), and hover: inside
         each entry the corpus recognizes the game's own StepRequest and
         StepResponse.

      3. Every top-level entry is the same field, 42 — our captures. Pin
         its type: on the field, `o` prefills an `override ... --as-new
         Capture`; tailor the name, Enter, `t` to apply. Now the entries
         read as a repeated Capture.

      4. Find the `generation` field and name it the same way: `o` for a
         prefilled override, tailor, Enter.

      5. Go to the non-canonical fields — the strings the client's schema
         never declared. Where one is set it reads "whoami" or
         "experiment": Eve's contraband. Name that field `contraband` with
         `o` again.

      All done: a schema reverse-crafted from a truncated, type-less blob,
      and Eve's covert channel read straight out of her own log.

      👋 Type `:q` to quit protolens.
    node: /
